---
import TrustPage from '../components/TrustPage.astro';
import { trust } from '../data/trust';
---

<TrustPage
  title="Privacy"
  description="What geurtsgaming.com and its arcade demo collect, what they do not, and how we keep children's information private."
  heading="Privacy"
  lede="You can play here without telling us who you are. This page says exactly what the site and its arcade demo do with information, in plain words."
>
  <div class="summary">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No accounts.</strong> We never ask for a name, an email address, a birthday or a photo.</li>
      <li><strong>The grade question stays in the game.</strong> The demo asks what grade you are in so the questions fit. The answer is used for that visit only. It is not saved and it is not sent anywhere.</li>
      <li><strong>No ads, and nothing sold.</strong> We do not show advertising here, and we do not sell or share information about the people who play.</li>
      <li><strong>Visits are counted.</strong> We use Google Analytics to see how many people visit, with its advertising features switched off.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Who this page covers</h2>
  <p>
    This page is about geurtsgaming.com and the arcade demo that plays on its home page. Our other games,
    Cool Typing Games and Earl vs. The Mutants, run on their own sites and stores and have their own terms.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
  <p>
    There is nowhere on this site to type your name, email address, age, school or address, and no way to upload
    a photo, a recording or a message to other players. The demo has no chat. We do not use the camera, the
    microphone or your location.
  </p>

  <h2>The arcade demo</h2>

  <h3>Your grade</h3>
  <p>
    Before the first challenge the demo asks which grades you are in (kindergarten to 2, 3 to 5, or 6 and up).
    That choice sets how hard the sums and typing lines are and how long you get. It is held in the game while
    the page is open and is gone when you close it. It is never written to your device and never leaves it.
  </p>

  <h3>What the demo keeps on your device</h3>
  <p>So that the game remembers you next time, your browser stores four things on your own device:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>whether sound is on or off;</li>
    <li>your best score;</li>
    <li>a made-up pilot callsign the game picks for you, such as NOVA-7;</li>
    <li>the Top 10 scores this browser has seen.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Clearing this site's data in your browser removes all of them.</p>

  <h3>What the demo sends to our game server</h3>
  <p>While the page is open, the game tells our game server that a pilot is there, so it can show how many pilots are online and draw other pilots' ships. It sends:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>a random pilot number, made new for each browser tab;</li>
    <li>the made-up callsign;</li>
    <li>while you are flying a wave: which wave it is, your score, how many people you have freed and where your ship is on the screen.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Other players can see the callsign and the ship. None of it says who you are, and the server forgets a pilot
    about two minutes after they leave. A finished game's score, wave and callsign may also be sent for the Top 10 board.
  </p>

  <h3>Voices</h3>
  <p>
    The commander, the boss and the pilot speak using the voices built in to your own device. The words are
    turned into speech on the device. Nothing is sent to us or to anyone else to do it.
  </p>

  <h2>Counting visits</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics to understand how the site is used: how many people visit a page, roughly where in
    the world they are (worked out from the internet address, which Google says Analytics does not store), and
    what kind of device and browser they use. We have set it up so that:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>its advertising features and Google signals are off;</li>
    <li>nothing it collects is used to personalise advertising;</li>
    <li>the only cookies it sets belong to this site, and they are deleted when you close your browser.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We use these numbers to improve the site. We do not use them to build a profile of anyone.</p>

  <h2>The companies that help us run the site</h2>
  <p>
    GitHub hosts the pages and Amazon Web Services runs the game server. Like any website, both receive your
    internet address in order to send you the page. We do not record it or connect it to anything else.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our games are made for children, so we built this site to follow the Children's Online Privacy Protection
    Act (COPPA): it does not ask children for personal information, and it does not need any to work.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are a parent or guardian and you have a question, or you believe a child has given us personal
    information, write to <a href={`mailto:${trust.email}`}>{trust.email}</a>. We will tell you what we have, if
    anything, and delete it if you ask.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Clear this site's data in your browser to remove the callsign and scores it has saved.</li>
    <li>Block cookies for this site if you would rather not be counted. Everything still works.</li>
    <li>Use the Sound button in the demo to turn off the sound effects and the voices.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Links to other places</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to our games and to stores such as Steam. Those sites have their own privacy policies, and
    this page does not cover them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If what the site does changes, this page changes first, and the date below changes with it.</p>
</TrustPage>
